{"post": {"source_id": "dev-x-0050", "platform": "x", "url": null, "posted_at": "2026-10-23T14:15:00Z", "author": {"handle": "@alpha_rider", "platform_user_id": "1001", "display_name": "Alpha Rider"}, "text": "Weekly macro thread. The Fed held rates again and the dot plot still shows two cuts next year, which the market had mostly priced in. Dollar index is drifting lower, which historically has been a tailwind for risk assets, but correlation between $BTC and the Nasdaq has been unstable since spring. Funding rates on perps are neutral, open interest is flat, and stablecoin supply on exchanges ticked up about 3% week over week. On-chain, long-term holder supply keeps rising while short-term holders are roughly at break-even, so there is no obvious capitulation or euphoria signal. $ETH staking ratio hit a new high. Honestly this looks like a range market to me and I am not making any moves until we get a clearer picture after the CPI print. Stay patient, manage risk, and don't let boredom make your decisions.", "context": {"kind": "original", "parent_text": null, "parent_author_handle": null, "quoted_text": null, "quoted_author_handle": null}}, "gold": {"label": "NO_NEW_BUY", "assets": [], "tags": ["long_post"], "notes": null}}
{"post": {"source_id": "dev-x-0051", "platform": "x", "url": null, "posted_at": "2026-10-24T21:15:00Z", "author": {"handle": "@satsmaxi_kai", "platform_user_id": "1002", "display_name": "Kai"}, "text": "Long thread on decentralized AI, because I keep getting asked. First, most 'AI coins' are a ticker and a logo with no product, and I think 90% of them go to zero. Second, the projects worth watching actually pay for compute or data and have real usage you can see on-chain. Third, valuations are stretched across the board, so position sizing matters more than picking. I've looked at subnets, emissions, validator economics and the dev activity for months now. So my plan: I'm accumulating $TAO between 380 and 420 and will keep adding on any flush below that. Everything else in the sector I'm ignoring for now. Fourth, expect brutal drawdowns, this sector moves 30% in a week both ways. Not advice, do your own research, and never size into something you can't hold through a 50% drop.", "context": {"kind": "original", "parent_text": null, "parent_author_handle": null, "quoted_text": null, "quoted_author_handle": null}}, "gold": {"label": "BUY", "assets": ["TAO"], "tags": ["long_post", "explicit"], "notes": null}}
{"post": {"source_id": "dev-x-0052", "platform": "x", "url": null, "posted_at": "2026-10-25T04:15:00Z", "author": {"handle": "@degenlens", "platform_user_id": "1003", "display_name": "Degen Lens"}, "text": "One year recap. Last November I told everyone to buy $SOL at 22 and got laughed at. I also called the $JUP airdrop farming meta early and wrote a full guide on it. Some calls were bad: my $APT entry was early and I sat through a 40% drawdown. Lessons: size smaller, take partial profits, and write down your invalidation before entering. Right now I'm still holding my core $SOL and $ETH positions and mostly sitting in stables otherwise. I'll post the full spreadsheet of every call I made this year so you can check my track record yourselves. Thanks for following along, it's been a wild year and I appreciate everyone who stuck around through the boring months.", "context": {"kind": "original", "parent_text": null, "parent_author_handle": null, "quoted_text": null, "quoted_author_handle": null}}, "gold": {"label": "NO_NEW_BUY", "assets": [], "tags": ["long_post", "retrospective", "existing_position"], "notes": null}}
